  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1224 PM Saturday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Seasonal temperatures and dry conditions into\nearly next week. Temperatures will gradually trend above normal\nby the middle of next week, perhaps nearing record highs late \nin the week.\n\nAn early season Nor'easter presently offshore of the Mid-Atlantic \nstates will continue to retrograde northwest into New Jersey over \nthe next 24-48 hours. It will linger into the early part of next \nweek, favoring continued seasonal temperatures in the upper 70s to \nlow 80s through Monday. Tuesday is a transition day when the system \nbegins to exit New England. \n\nCome midweek, high pressure ridging will build back in and promote a \nwarming trend to above normal highs, especially late in the week. \nLate next week, guidance is indicating a return to some humid air in \nthe southerly return flow. Add to that, low-level thicknesses may \nexceed 1420m, typical values seen in July. This should favor \nmid/upper 80s to even a few low 90s in spots as we close out \nnext week. A few sites may get close to record highs during this\nstretch.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... Overall dry weather through the period, with some \nsignals for increased rain chances perhaps next weekend.\n\nThe pattern continues to favor dry conditions well into next week. \nThe latest ensemble and probabilistic guidance has slowed any onset \nof unsettled weather to perhaps not until the upcoming weekend. With \nridging set to build back in midweek and some ensemble clusters \nshowing that pattern persisting into late next week, our rain \nchances may have to wait until more appreciable Gulf moisture can \nbuild back in sometime late Friday or even Sat-Sun next weekend. For \nnow, only a slight to low chance of rain is expected Fri-Sat. A \nfrontal system could approach late in the weekend, favoring a better \nchance of unsettled weather, but the pattern is quite uncertain at \nthis point.",
